{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Close attempt (sanctioned non-force path) — STILL OPEN.\n\n1) 'rebar transition 5dd2-e4a6-4189-486d open closed' failed with:\n   plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation. Run rebar review-plan 5dd2-e4a6-4189-486d separately, then retry close.\n\n2) Ran the legitimate remedy 'rebar review-plan 5dd2-e4a6-4189-486d' (no --force). Verdict: BLOCK, 7 blocking findings, signature {signed: false, reason: BLOCK}. Every finding says the same thing, from a different criterion:\n   - E4 / G6 (x2): the plan is a NO-OP — every gate-level surface it names as mislabeled 'three-pass' already reads 'four-pass (find -> verify -> decide -> coach)'. The problem the plan describes no longer exists.\n   - G1G2 / T8 (x2 each): the Scope line anchors are stale and point at unrelated code — 'src/rebar/mcp_server.py:657 (review_plan docstring)' is a register_llm_tools(mcp, ctx) call (the docstring now lives at src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:195), and '_llm_commands.py:215,225 (CLI help)' points at the --graph argument help and a parser.error call (the real four-pass help is at _llm_commands.py:498).\n\nSo the gate is blocking precisely BECAUSE the work is already done: the plan-review gate reviews a plan against current reality, and a completed ticket's plan reads as divergent-from-reality. Per the operator's instruction I did not use --force on review-plan or --force-close on the transition.\n\nTo unlock a close without a bypass, someone must decide between: (a) rewriting this ticket's What/Scope in the past tense with corrected anchors (mcp_server.py:657 -> _mcp_llm.py:195; _llm_commands.py:215,225 -> :484,:498) and re-running review-plan, which is the documented 'when the acceptance criteria no longer match reality' remedy in docs/plan-review-gate.md; or (b) an operator --force-close, which is explicitly out of scope for this task. All four ACs are verified and ticked (see the preceding comment); only the plan-review close gate stands in the way."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786086247125718001,"uuid":"9364bb33-aac3-4aa5-a0c7-2b61713dd59e"}